=== python/mypy#14122
{"body":"Currently we don't handle `__call__()` on metaclasses correctly. For example:\r\n\r\n```python\r\nclass M(type):\r\n    def __call__(self, x: int) -\u003e Any: ...\r\n\r\nclass C(metaclass=M): ...\r\n\r\nC(x=1)\r\n```\r\nresults in a false positive. Also similarly handling of metaclass `__call__()` in protocols is not very principled, see e.g. https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/14121","closedAt":null,"labels":["bug","priority-2-low","topic-protocols"],"number":14122,"state":"OPEN","stateReason":"","title":"Support __call__ on metaclasses","url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/14122"}
